# C# Conventions

- Prefer primary constructors for dependency-focused classes.
- Keep nullable reference types enabled; avoid `!` unless briefly justified inline.
- Keep flows async end-to-end; avoid `.Result` and `.Wait()`.
- Pass `CancellationToken` through I/O paths (API calls, DB operations, background jobs).
- Prefer EF Core for persistence; use raw SQL only when necessary and document why.
- Use structured logging fields for sync failures (source, external id, reason).
- Keep adapters and mappers small and composable.
